A||||5||JohnnyK||Sways dangerously at 5mph||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||05-31-2000||04:49 PM||||Sort of the same problem as Cutter, but happens even at the lowest speed. Almost feels like a tire is flat and wobbling on the rim (Pressures are good).. It didn't do it one day, and then the next day it is.. I hear that my upper a-arm bushings are floping around, but I'm sure it would have done it the day before to. Feels REALLY unsafe, like a boat, but worse.  Could it be the sway bar or anything? Steering wheel doesn't really vibrate or anything.. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-31-2000||08:07 PM||||Almost sounds like one of the tires has a belt that shifted. If it's on the back, the whole back of the car can wobble back and forth. Will be most noticeable at low speeds. After you get up to higher speeds, it would feel more like a vibration. Probably won't feel it in the steering wheel unless it's on the front. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||06-01-2000||01:32 AM||||Last summer my mechanic worked on an 87 coupe. When he initally test drove it, it would sway left and right dangerously at any speed (we wouldn't take it above 15 or 20). His job was to replace the engine with a lower mileage engine. He found that the sway was caused by some nimrod installing the wrong (smaller) bolts from the struts to the A-arm. I think the A-arm, I'm no mechanic, but when he took the wheel off, the whole set up would wobble around. Kinda scary!!!<BR>Good luck!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||06-01-2000||01:41 AM||||Are your lug nuts tight?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||06-01-2000||01:44 AM||||Jack the front up and put it on stands...Start moving the wheels around looking for moving parts that shouldn't move. Use a pinch bar or lever to move a-arms and check for bushing wear. Maybe a balljoint has blown out. Check inner / outer tie rod ends and steering rack for wear.<P>Ozzy<P>P.S. Checks Ed's suggestion thoroughly too. I had my nephew change out rims on my Coupe once. He swore he tightened them properly...2 days later my wife tells me "there's a funny noise in back of the car". I was not even thinking lugnuts...Bigger 'n' sh*t! All five rear right loose with a wobbling rim. She is VERY lucky the wheel did not come off on the highway. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Ozzy (edited 06-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||06-01-2000||01:48 PM||||Well, you guys forgot to mention the (sort of) obvious.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> THe whole frame basically snapped where the lower rear a-arm connects to it.. I guess I get to scrap the car even though I have never really driven it..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
